ility":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.3960196232979099,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.047620002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":31.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"GRAIL, Inc., a commercial-stage healthcare company, provides multi-cancer early detection testing and services in the United States and internationally. It offers Galleri, a cancer screening test for asymptomatic individuals over 50 years of age; and a diagnostic aid for cancer tests to accelerate diagnostic resolution for patients with clinical suspicion of cancer. The company also provides development services, including support for ongoing clinical studies, pilot testing, research, and therapy development. In addition, its precision oncology portfolio consists of n RUO-targeted methylation-based platform that enables applications for disease prognostication, risk stratification, minimal residual disease detection, and recurrence and relapse monitoring. The company was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Joshua J. Ofman M.D., M.S.H.S | CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 910 people. Revenue per employee of $162K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $64K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["GRAIL, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $5.2B market cap on $147M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -71% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $300M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 40% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 382% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $14.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 177% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Contrast: GRAIL (GRAL) versus Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/financial-contrast-grail-gral-versus-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794496574.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GRAIL Inc (GRAL) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: FDA Nod on the Horizon as Galleri Gains ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/grail-inc-gral-q3-2026-010555245.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794272755.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","regulatory"]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in GRAL Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_GRAL_Response_110826093602_1794148562.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794148562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What GRAIL (GRAL) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/what-grail-gral-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794086118.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"GRAIL (GRAL) Could Be 8% Undervalued On Galleri FDA Momentum","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.